> **wallhack** (plural **wallhacks**)
>
> *(video games)* A patch enabling a player to cheat by modifying the properties of walls, as by making them transparent or nonsolid.

Layer 3 tunneling tool for network pivoting in penetration testing scenarios.

## Performance

{% grid  %}
{% card title="QUIC Transport" icon="wifi" %}
- **Single stream:** 2.9 Gbps
- **2 streams:** 2.9 Gbps
- **4 streams:** 2.5 Gbps
- **Reverse:** 893 Mbps
{% /card %}
{% card title="WebSocket Transport (TLS)" icon="plug" %}
- **Single stream:** 4.3 Gbps
- **2 streams:** 4.0 Gbps
- **4 streams:** 3.8 Gbps
{% /card %}
{% /grid %}

{% callout type="note" %}
Benchmarks measured with iperf3 over isolated network namespaces with veth pairs. Real-world performance varies with network conditions.
{% /callout %}

## Binary Size

| Target | Size |
|--------|------|
| Linux x64 (musl, static) | **4.9 MB** |
| Linux x64 (glibc, dynamic) | 4.9 MB |

### Quick Install

{% codeblock code="cargo install wallhack" /%}
